<section class="container compare">
  <div class="intro">
    <h2>How it compares to what you use now.</h2>
    <p>
      Nearhost is for your own machines and your own browser. It is the wrong tool for showing work
      to someone else.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="rows">
    <div class="row">
      <h3>
        <code>ssh -L</code> by hand
      </h3>
      <p>
        The same OpenSSH forwards, typed per port and retyped after every dropped connection, with
        no hostname and no certificate.
      </p>
      <p class="diff">
        Nearhost keeps one supervised SSH connection per server, adds and removes forwards while it
        runs, and puts a trusted <code>https://name.test</code> in front.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <h3>Editor port forwarding</h3>
      <p>
        Convenient while the editor window is open. You get <code>localhost:port</code> URLs, so
        cookies and OAuth settings differ from a named HTTPS origin.
      </p>
      <p class="diff">
        Nearhost runs in a terminal, independent of any editor, and each project keeps the same
        HTTPS name every day.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <h3>A VPN or mesh network</h3>
      <p>
        Makes the machine reachable, which means an agent on every machine and a dev server that
        listens beyond <code>localhost</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="diff">
        Nearhost installs nothing on the server. The dev server keeps listening on{' '}
        <code>localhost</code> and is reached over SSH.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <h3>A public tunnel service</h3>
      <p>
        Built for sharing. Your traffic goes through someone else's relay to a public URL, usually
        behind an account.
      </p>
      <p class="diff">
        Nearhost has no relay, no account and no public URL. Use a tunnel service when a client
        needs to see the page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .compare {
    padding-block: var(--nh-section);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--nh-font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: var(--nh-track-display);
  }
  .intro p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--nh-body);
    font-size: 18px;
  }
  .rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--nh-line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: 28px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--nh-line);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .row:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .row p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--nh-muted);
    font-size: 15.5px;
  }
  .row .diff {
    color: var(--nh-text);
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--nh-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 719px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 10px;
      padding: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
